* Hermetic ngspice init for sim/phase-noise.
*
* Every run_*.sh in this directory copies this file into the scratch directory
* it runs ngspice from, so a run does NOT depend on whether $HOME/.spiceinit
* exists (the PDK ships libs.tech/ngspice/install.py, which symlinks one into
* $HOME; a cold-start checkout on a machine where that was never run must
* still reproduce the committed numbers).
*
* ngbehavior=hsa is the compatibility mode the PDK's own .spiceinit sets and
* the mode its model libraries are written against. It is load-bearing on the
* PDK-dependent decks here for the same reason it is in
* sim/oscillator-core/.spiceinit: design/vco.spice instantiates npn13G2v,
* cap_cmim and sg13_hv_svaricap, whose model cards use HSPICE-style
* constructs ngspice only accepts in this mode.
*
* run_method_check.sh copies it too, even though its synthetic decks use only
* ngspice-native L/C/R and behavioural sources and do not need the mode: the
* method check exists to validate the SAME extractors the measured run grades
* with, so it runs under the same ngspice configuration rather than quietly
* diverging from it.
set ngbehavior=hsa
